      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "How to find the V"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After completing a row, look at each dc from the front. You will see a horizontal pair of loops at the top (the normal insertion point) and below them a V-shape made by the two slanted legs of the stitch. Insert the hook through both legs of this V."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12 ws x 14 rows = 10 x 10 cm in aran with a 6 mm hook. The V insertion is tighter than a normal dc, so gauge is tighter despite the larger hook."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
